<h2 id="5-the-campus-bridge">5. The Campus Bridge</h2>
<p>Back to our own university college campus. In order to connect the campus with the other side of the busy national road that leads to more parking options and another connecting road to the northern part of Limburg, 1500 tonnes of steel was brought in via the aforementioned Albert Canal to create the Campus Bridge. This dramatically reduced conflicts of the intersection for pedestrians and cyclists and should find a connection with the <em>F</em> cycling highways nearby&mdash;the road and infrastructure up to the bridge is currently being rebuilt.</p>
<p>The bridge looks more impressive from a certain height as explained on the <a href="https://wegenenverkeer.be/werken/campusbrug-aan-grote-ring-x-elfde-liniestraat">agency for roads &amp; traffic website</a>. Even though in the photo below it looks like a classic bridge spanning at most 50 metres to cover five car lanes, you&rsquo;ll be cycling for almost half a kilometre (410 metres) to cross it!</p>
<p>
